---
import ThemeToggle from "@/components/ThemeToggle.astro";

/**
 * The site footer (#91): a generic copyright, set in the editorial face on
 * the editorial ground, paired with the theme override control (#92).
 *
 * BaseLayout renders this outside .screen, so it is the page's single
 * contentinfo landmark and is identical across page types. /chat opts out
 * via footer={false}: it is the full-window slab, with no editorial ground.
 * That opt-out is also what removes the theme control from /chat, which is
 * correct by design (the expanded slab is always-night, so the control would
 * visibly do nothing there).
 *
 * The row (#101): copyright left, control right, one flex line. The control
 * used to be a FIXED chip bottom-right, which occluded live body text through
 * the whole scroll on mobile (the content column nearly fills a 390px
 * viewport, so an opaque overlay anchored to the viewport is never clear of
 * the text). Docking it here removes the entire occlusion class rather than
 * mitigating it: an in-flow element cannot overlap anything. It wraps to two
 * lines only if the row cannot fit, which at the narrowest realistic viewport
 * (320px) it does not need to.
 *
 * The year is literal on purpose (Brian's exact string). Deriving it from the
 * build date would self-maintain, but that is his call to make, not ours.
 */
---

<footer class="sfoot">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p>&copy; 2026 Brian Rohde</p>
    <ThemeToggle />
  </div>
</footer>
